# `for (const [key, count] of counts)` walks the table of the map in line, without an iterator object and without a result object.
# Each turn makes the pair of key and value as an array, asks which storage that array has, and reads the two elements back with a test of the length in front of each.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="total" role=Source
# CHECK: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll{{*}}:LoopHint)
# CHECK: Load(b@{{*}}Reads:CollectionEntries, {{*}}:MapNext)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[pair]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}:NewArray)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load8Z(b@[[pair]], offset = 4, ControlDependent|Reads:JSCell_indexingTypeAndMisc, {{*}}:HasArrayStorage)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[storage]] = Load(b@[[pair]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSObject_butterfly, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[storage]], ControlDependent|Reads:indexedDoubleProperties_0, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedDoubleProperties_1, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The two patchpoints on the likely paths are the poll and the allocation.
# The function has calls, and Windows passes arguments in other registers: its count is not checked.
# X64: instructions: 75, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 59
# ARM64: instructions: 87, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 69
